# telegram-public.env — environment for the Hathor PUBLIC Telegram bot.
# Copy to the operator's private env path on the box and fill in the values.
# Ships with placeholders / blanks ONLY — no real hostnames, paths, or tokens in the repo.
#
# There are NO chain keys here. The ONLY secret is the Telegram bot token, which can only
# send/receive Telegram messages — it can never sign or broadcast anything on-chain.
# Keep this file chmod 600, in the operator's private path, NEVER committed.

# --- THE ONE THING TO GO LIVE ----------------------------------------------
# The public bot's token from @BotFather (create a NEW bot, distinct from any private/operator
# bot and from the watcher's alert bot). Leave EMPTY and the service runs idle (logs
# "...public bot idle." and exits cleanly) — so you can install + enable the unit BEFORE the
# token exists. Drop the token here and `systemctl restart` to go live.
TELEGRAM_PUBLIC_BOT_TOKEN=

# --- chain (read-only, for /status) ----------------------------------------
# Local MELEK testnet RPC — read-only JSON-RPC the node on the box serves. Used by /status,
# /hathor, /block, /witness, /account, /feed. If unset/unreachable, those commands soft-fail
# (the bot still answers /price, /clarity, /help, etc.). Testnet output is always labeled
# "[TestNet not MELEK]" — that label travels in the message itself.
MELEK_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090
# testnet | mainnet — controls the network label. Default testnet (the live network today).
MELEK_NETWORK=testnet

# --- optional display -------------------------------------------------------
# Public site shown in the welcome / help footer. Defaults to the public SoapBox aggregator.
# SOAPBOX_SITE=https://data.soapbox.community
